1233
01:20:42,242 --> 01:20:44,779
<i>♪ Baby Jane, I lost my nerve ♪</i>

1234
01:20:44,878 --> 01:20:48,215
<i>♪ Hear my heart</i>
<i>Please ignore my words ♪</i>

1235
01:20:48,315 --> 01:20:50,819
<i>♪ We jumped the broom</i>
<i>That was the best of days ♪</i>

1236
01:20:52,252 --> 01:20:55,889
<i>♪ Since we broke up</i>
<i>I've been in a daze ♪</i>

1237
01:20:55,989 --> 01:20:59,460
<i>♪ Baby Jane</i>
<i>Please don't take the cat ♪</i>

1238
01:21:08,369 --> 01:21:10,037
<i>Welcome</i>
<i>to the Rhinestone Chalet,</i>

1239
01:21:10,137 --> 01:21:12,607
<i>Moretti's childhood home</i>
<i>turned interactive museum.</i>

1240
01:21:12,707 --> 01:21:15,510
<i>Did you know</i>
<i>that Alfred's roots</i>
<i>come from Peoria, Illinois?</i>

1241
01:21:15,610 --> 01:21:18,479
<i>...feel to you until that day.</i>

1242
01:21:18,580 --> 01:21:19,647
<i>I mean, until that moment.</i>

1243
01:21:24,619 --> 01:21:26,554
Circle back around.

1244
01:22:19,874 --> 01:22:21,008
So jealous.

1245
01:22:34,188 --> 01:22:36,056
You're still pretty.

1246
01:25:01,703 --> 01:25:06,608
...sacrifice of
our beautiful creation.

1247
01:25:06,708 --> 01:25:10,277
See, we can't, uh,
un-paint a canvas

1248
01:25:10,377 --> 01:25:13,948
or un-play a chord.

1249
01:25:14,048 --> 01:25:16,784
And if a mistake has been made,

1250
01:25:16,884 --> 01:25:19,252
either yours or someone else's,

1251
01:25:19,353 --> 01:25:21,455
the only way to rectify it

1252
01:25:21,556 --> 01:25:25,793
is to make something beautiful.

1253
01:25:27,461 --> 01:25:32,033
Now, I've studied
at every temple of taste

1254
01:25:32,132 --> 01:25:34,401
in the entire world.

1255
01:25:34,501 --> 01:25:38,673
I've picked over
every reliquary that exists.

1256
01:25:38,773 --> 01:25:44,879
But I've never seen anything
as beautiful as you pearls.

1257
01:25:50,118 --> 01:25:54,055
We don't know
what tomorrow will bring.

1258
01:25:54,154 --> 01:25:55,322
Maybe we'll all be together...

1259
01:25:59,159 --> 01:26:00,828
Listen to me.

1260
01:26:00,928 --> 01:26:03,931
When you get to the gate,
make a right, okay?

1261
01:26:05,399 --> 01:26:08,603
And then, go until you see
the light, all right?

1262
01:26:10,270 --> 01:26:13,206
But let's hope
it's something beautiful.

1263
01:26:13,306 --> 01:26:15,342
To our time in the sand.

1264
01:26:15,442 --> 01:26:17,612
To our time
in the sand.

1265
01:26:17,712 --> 01:26:19,312
Push me.

1266
01:26:19,814 --> 01:26:20,915
Cheers.

1267
01:26:28,388 --> 01:26:29,757
Cheers.

1268
01:28:12,160 --> 01:28:13,561
Hey.

1269
01:28:14,228 --> 01:28:15,462
Help, help, help!

1270
01:28:15,563 --> 01:28:17,532
-Who are you?
-I was in the house.

1271
01:28:17,632 --> 01:28:20,300
I was there,
and people are dead,
and we have to go.

1272
01:28:20,400 --> 01:28:23,403
- You were in there?
- Yes, I was in there.

1273
01:28:23,503 --> 01:28:25,472
Holy shit, you're bleeding.
Are you hurt?

1274
01:28:25,573 --> 01:28:27,608
-Yes, I am hurt!
-Is Moretti hurt?

1275
01:28:28,676 --> 01:28:30,545
Yes, he's hurt,
so we have to go.

1276
01:28:30,645 --> 01:28:32,213
-You met Moretti?
-We have to leave.

1277
01:28:32,312 --> 01:28:33,815
Wait, did he do the wiggle?

1278
01:28:33,915 --> 01:28:35,116
I bet he did the wiggle.

1279
01:28:35,216 --> 01:28:36,818
Did you hear
the new song...

1280
01:28:36,918 --> 01:28:38,351
I'm so sorry!

1281
01:29:36,110 --> 01:29:39,614
<i>Do you think</i>
<i>about why that Levelist</i>
<i>helped you escape that night?</i>

1282
01:29:39,714 --> 01:29:41,916
Or do you mentally try not
to go back to that time?

1283
01:29:44,352 --> 01:29:45,953
Maybe a mix of both.
I don't know.

1284
01:29:46,053 --> 01:29:48,289
I'm... This is, like,
my millionth interview
this month,

1285
01:29:48,388 --> 01:29:49,891
so you have to forgive me.

1286
01:29:49,991 --> 01:29:51,092
Book tours are...

1287
01:29:52,026 --> 01:29:52,960
Exhausting.

1288
01:29:53,060 --> 01:29:55,963
- Yeah, exhausting.
- Yes, I'm tired.

1289
01:29:56,063 --> 01:30:00,301
So, you know I gotta ask...

1290
01:30:00,400 --> 01:30:03,838
Is that how it really happened
when you went back
to the compound?

1291
01:30:03,938 --> 01:30:05,773
It's... it's exactly
as I wrote it.

1292
01:30:50,518 --> 01:30:53,120
<i>And he was actually</i>
<i>just sitting there alone,</i>

1293
01:30:53,220 --> 01:30:56,757
<i>still in the white suit,</i>
<i>playing the piano?</i>

1294
01:30:56,857 --> 01:31:01,128
I do feel like I've said this
a million times at this point,

1295
01:31:01,228 --> 01:31:04,198
but it was, uh, surreal.

1296
01:31:04,298 --> 01:31:08,102
Cops haven't been able to
locate a single Levelist body.

1297
01:31:08,202 --> 01:31:10,404
They still haven't found
the fan who was at the gate.

1298
01:31:10,503 --> 01:31:12,239
-Just nothing.
-Hmm.

1299
01:31:12,340 --> 01:31:13,908
Um, sorry.

1300
01:31:15,876 --> 01:31:17,745
-Do you mind if I...
-Oh, yeah.

1301
01:31:17,845 --> 01:31:19,013
Thanks.

1302
01:31:21,248 --> 01:31:22,550
Hello? This is Ariel Ecton.

1303
01:31:22,650 --> 01:31:24,018
Ariel. Guess who.

1304
01:31:24,118 --> 01:31:26,687
It's Soledad Yusef
calling from sunny
Malibu, California.

1305
01:31:26,787 --> 01:31:29,023
<i>And how do you find yourself</i>
<i>this Monday morning?</i>

1306
01:31:31,625 --> 01:31:33,027
My love? Hello?

1307
01:31:33,127 --> 01:31:36,697
-What do you want?
-Ooh. Someone's spicy
this morning.

1308
01:31:37,965 --> 01:31:41,235
But I believe it's more
of what you want.

1309
01:31:41,335 --> 01:31:42,837
<i>Didn't you send in</i>

1310
01:31:42,937 --> 01:31:45,506
six interview requests
to sit down with Mr. Moretti
for your novel?

1311
01:31:45,606 --> 01:31:48,743
<i>Well, you're in luck.</i>
<i>Mr. Moretti would like</i>
<i>to sit down this evening</i>

1312
01:31:48,843 --> 01:31:50,845
<i>at the high-risk</i>
<i>state hospital in Reno.</i>

1313
01:31:50,945 --> 01:31:53,180
<i>It's like a medieval torture</i>
<i>chamber, if you ask me.</i>

1314
01:31:53,280 --> 01:31:55,316
Honestly, these states
should be tried for the way
they treat people.

1315
01:31:55,416 --> 01:31:57,284
It's just absolutely abhorrent.

1316
01:31:57,385 --> 01:31:58,886
<i>Soledad, you are aware</i>

1317
01:31:58,986 --> 01:32:00,521
that your client,
Alfred Moretti,

1318
01:32:00,621 --> 01:32:03,457
pled guilty to the murder
of five innocent people,

1319
01:32:03,557 --> 01:32:05,760
tried to kill me,
and is suspected

1320
01:32:05,860 --> 01:32:08,896
<i>of leading hundreds</i>
<i>of Levelists to mass suicide?</i>

1321
01:32:08,996 --> 01:32:09,964
He's passionate.

1322
01:32:11,298 --> 01:32:13,634
<i>Ciao, my darling.</i>
<i>Take care of yourself.</i>

1323
01:32:29,450 --> 01:32:32,119
Salutations, as they say.

1324
01:32:50,271 --> 01:32:51,839
Oh, heavy.

1325
01:32:53,307 --> 01:32:54,708
Shall we get started?

1326
01:33:00,081 --> 01:33:01,882
Python.

1327
01:33:01,982 --> 01:33:05,252
-Excuse me?
-Well, in your novel,
you wrote that when...

1328
01:33:05,352 --> 01:33:07,288
the first day we met

1329
01:33:07,388 --> 01:33:11,258
that I was wearing
cream-colored alligator boots,

1330
01:33:11,358 --> 01:33:15,129
but in fact, they were
smoke-colored python boots.

1331
01:33:15,229 --> 01:33:19,100
Now, of course,
that's an easy mistake to make
for an untrained eye,

1332
01:33:19,200 --> 01:33:22,369
but, uh, I would never.
It's unimaginable--

1333
01:33:22,470 --> 01:33:24,238
In my "novel," you said?

1334
01:33:25,039 --> 01:33:28,142
In my 320-page non-fiction text,

1335
01:33:28,242 --> 01:33:31,779
your biggest gripe is with
the material of your boots?

1336
01:33:31,879 --> 01:33:35,316
You know, it's just, a little
constructive criticism

1337
01:33:35,416 --> 01:33:37,885
never killed anyone, Ariel.

1338
01:33:41,355 --> 01:33:42,524
Okay.

1339
01:33:42,623 --> 01:33:44,692
Um...

1340
01:33:47,328 --> 01:33:50,831
I didn't expect you
to be remorseful
like a normal person,

1341
01:33:50,931 --> 01:33:54,869
but I came here
to try to report the truth

1342
01:33:54,969 --> 01:33:56,637
so that there's closure
for the families and--

1343
01:33:56,737 --> 01:33:59,173
And to sell a few more books.

1344
01:33:59,273 --> 01:34:03,410
-Well...
-Ariel, while you circle
around and around

1345
01:34:03,512 --> 01:34:06,213
the one question

1346
01:34:06,313 --> 01:34:11,620
that you most assuredly
came here to ask me...
Very quickly...

1347
01:34:11,719 --> 01:34:14,688
Primitive man chose their leader

1348
01:34:14,788 --> 01:34:19,026
in the same way that
animals chose their leader...

1349
01:34:19,760 --> 01:34:21,162
uh, brute strength.

1350
01:34:21,262 --> 01:34:24,198
Yeah, I... I'm familiar
with Darwin's theory.

1351
01:34:24,298 --> 01:34:28,135
Uh, what does that have to do
with you being a murderer?

1352
01:34:29,538 --> 01:34:32,072
Man evolved.

1353
01:34:32,173 --> 01:34:33,374
Humanity evolved.

1354
01:34:33,474 --> 01:34:37,378
Um, it, uh, created government

1355
01:34:37,478 --> 01:34:39,180
and rules and law.

1356
01:34:39,280 --> 01:34:43,751
And with those things,
then the criteria

1357
01:34:43,851 --> 01:34:46,887
for what was needed
in a leader changed.

1358
01:34:46,987 --> 01:34:51,225
So, it went from this
to left brain.

1359
01:34:51,325 --> 01:34:55,162
To be president,
you have to go
to an Ivy League school

1360
01:34:55,262 --> 01:34:57,965
and get a little Ivy League
law degree

1361
01:34:58,065 --> 01:35:02,537
to signal to the rest of us,
the peons,

1362
01:35:02,637 --> 01:35:05,372
uh, that this is
the smart person.

1363
01:35:05,472 --> 01:35:07,074
But look at where we are.

1364
01:35:07,174 --> 01:35:10,144
Today's world is burning,
literally.

1365
01:35:10,244 --> 01:35:13,948
Illiteracy is at its highest.
We've never been more divided.

1366
01:35:14,048 --> 01:35:17,017
We have permanent war,
and the list goes on.

1367
01:35:17,117 --> 01:35:21,690
So, clearly, the metric,
this left-brain metric,

1368
01:35:21,789 --> 01:35:24,458
failed miserably.

1369
01:35:24,559 --> 01:35:27,494
But there is an answer.

1370
01:35:28,262 --> 01:35:30,231
A new evolution.

1371
01:35:31,332 --> 01:35:37,504
So, won't be this anymore
or this left brain

1372
01:35:37,606 --> 01:35:39,574
but this right brain

1373
01:35:39,674 --> 01:35:43,678
where the most creative
are in charge.

1374
01:35:43,777 --> 01:35:49,083
Look, I'm not just gonna
sit here and act like
I didn't find Stan's old article

1375
01:35:49,183 --> 01:35:51,986
where he referred to <i>Tilt</i>
as overrated,

1376
01:35:52,086 --> 01:35:55,557
Bianca's rather unflattering
paparazzi shots.

1377
01:35:55,657 --> 01:35:57,157
Not good. Not too pretty.

1378
01:35:57,258 --> 01:35:59,893
And let's not forget Clara's
digs about your bald head.

1379
01:35:59,994 --> 01:36:01,563
And even you can't
wiggle your way free

1380
01:36:01,663 --> 01:36:02,997
after murdering
hundreds of people.

1381
01:36:03,097 --> 01:36:05,099
I didn't murder
hundreds of people.

1382
01:36:05,199 --> 01:36:08,002
You didn't murder Stan Sullivan,
Clara Armstrong,

1383
01:36:08,102 --> 01:36:10,572
Bianca Tyson,
Emily Katz, and Bill Lotto?

1384
01:36:10,672 --> 01:36:12,406
Oh, yeah, I murdered them.

1385
01:36:13,708 --> 01:36:17,878
You should know
your masterpiece, Ariel,

1386
01:36:17,978 --> 01:36:22,116
is also the introduction
to our story.

1387
01:36:23,784 --> 01:36:25,553
No one will condone murder.

1388
01:36:27,488 --> 01:36:31,760
But if it's scandalous enough,
they'll never stop
talking about it.

1389
01:36:31,859 --> 01:36:34,895
Besides, you're not gonna stop
becoming Catholic

1390
01:36:34,995 --> 01:36:37,398
'cause you read a book
about the Crusades.

1391
01:36:37,498 --> 01:36:41,869
You're serving a life sentence
five times over.

1392
01:36:41,969 --> 01:36:44,838
Why not just tell us
where the bodies are?

1393
01:36:44,938 --> 01:36:46,574
Where are the Levelists?

1394
01:36:47,676 --> 01:36:49,443
Around.

1395
01:36:49,544 --> 01:36:54,882
<i>We're spread out,</i>
<i>but still connected</i>
<i>to teach the young</i>

1396
01:36:54,982 --> 01:36:57,151
<i>and sprout new chapters,</i>

1397
01:36:57,251 --> 01:36:59,587
<i>to preserve dying crafts,</i>

1398
01:36:59,688 --> 01:37:01,756
<i>to inspire and comfort,</i>

1399
01:37:01,855 --> 01:37:05,159
<i>to fan the flames</i>
<i>of raw enthusiasm,</i>

1400
01:37:05,259 --> 01:37:10,898
<i>to closely monitor those</i>
<i>who obstruct</i>
<i>the divinely burdened.</i>

1401
01:37:10,998 --> 01:37:13,668
<i>Not hiding but waiting.</i>

1402
01:37:13,768 --> 01:37:15,969
<i>Waiting to better tomorrow.</i>

1403
01:37:16,070 --> 01:37:19,239
So, what was in
the champagne glasses, then?

1404
01:37:21,275 --> 01:37:22,711
Champagne.

1405
01:37:22,811 --> 01:37:24,746
- Okay.
- Oh.

1406
01:37:24,845 --> 01:37:27,014
With talent comes forgiveness.

1407
01:37:27,114 --> 01:37:28,882
The bigger the talent,

1408
01:37:28,982 --> 01:37:31,586
the more complete
the forgiveness.

1409
01:37:32,620 --> 01:37:35,989
Level will grow and grow.

1410
01:37:37,891 --> 01:37:41,730
We just, uh...

1411
01:37:41,830 --> 01:37:44,865
needed someone
to get the ball rolling.

1412
01:37:44,965 --> 01:37:46,467
So, um...

1413
01:37:50,104 --> 01:37:51,740
Come on. You get it.

1414
01:37:54,875 --> 01:37:56,076
So, why me?

1415
01:37:56,176 --> 01:37:57,344
Disco.

1416
01:38:00,481 --> 01:38:02,517
Two reasons, really.

1417
01:38:03,518 --> 01:38:06,120
One for us, one for me.

1418
01:38:06,220 --> 01:38:08,989
For us, we felt
you were a pure vessel,

1419
01:38:09,089 --> 01:38:12,727
completely uncorrupted
by success,

1420
01:38:12,827 --> 01:38:15,864
uncorrupted by cheap shots
for clicks.

1421
01:38:15,996 --> 01:38:18,465
For me, while looking
through your background,

1422
01:38:18,566 --> 01:38:23,705
I read a story you'd written
about a school board lady.

1423
01:38:23,805 --> 01:38:25,939
- Remember that?
- Carol Reggo?

1424
01:38:26,039 --> 01:38:30,177
That piece was less
than 500 words. It was before
I was even at <i>J.</i>

1425
01:38:30,277 --> 01:38:34,716
You wrote that her chin was

1426
01:38:34,816 --> 01:38:38,218
"delightfully inconspicuous."

1427
01:38:40,120 --> 01:38:43,457
And I needed my chin
in good hands.

1428
01:38:56,704 --> 01:39:00,174
<i>Once in a generation,</i>
<i>a tragedy so compelling occurs,</i>

1429
01:39:00,274 --> 01:39:02,109
<i>it grabs the entire world's</i>
<i>attention.</i>

1430
01:39:02,209 --> 01:39:05,946
<i>Most people</i>
<i>condemn the horrific events</i>
<i>that took place a few years ago,</i>

1431
01:39:06,046 --> 01:39:09,183
<i>while a growing minority</i>
<i>sympathize with</i>
<i>the guilty party.</i>

1432
01:39:09,283 --> 01:39:14,254
<i>After all,</i> Caesar's Request
<i>has sold millions of copies</i>
<i>since its release.</i>

1433
01:39:14,354 --> 01:39:16,256
<i>But the one thing</i>
<i>we can all agree on...</i>

1434
01:39:16,356 --> 01:39:18,292
<i>Our next guest is a star.</i>

1435
01:39:18,392 --> 01:39:20,829
<i>Her new book</i>
<i>was an instant bestseller,</i>

1436
01:39:20,929 --> 01:39:23,898
but unless
you've been living on Mars,
you already know that.

1437
01:39:23,997 --> 01:39:26,266
Ms. Ecton, good morning.
Congratulations.

1438
01:39:26,366 --> 01:39:27,968
I'm so thrilled to be
sitting down with you today.

1439
01:39:28,068 --> 01:39:32,239
I mean, <i>Our Time in the Sand</i>
is such a daring,
beautiful novel.

1440
01:39:32,339 --> 01:39:36,210
What does it feel like
to have written the book
that everybody's talking about?

1441
01:39:42,617 --> 01:39:44,117
Ms. Ecton?

1442
01:40:10,712 --> 01:40:15,850
<i>♪ Congratulations on the mess</i>
<i>You made of things ♪</i>

1443
01:40:15,950 --> 01:40:21,556
<i>♪ I'm trying to reconstruct</i>
<i>The air and all that brings ♪</i>

1444
01:40:21,656 --> 01:40:26,226
<i>♪ And oxidation is</i>
<i>The compromise you own ♪</i>

1445
01:40:26,326 --> 01:40:28,395
<i>♪ But this is beginning</i>
<i>To feel ♪</i>

1446
01:40:28,495 --> 01:40:31,365
<i>♪ Like the dog wants a bone ♪</i>

1447
01:40:31,465 --> 01:40:32,834
<i>♪ Say ♪</i>

1448
01:40:32,934 --> 01:40:38,105
<i>♪ La, la, la, la</i>
<i>La, la, la, la ♪</i>

1449
01:40:38,205 --> 01:40:43,578
<i>♪ La, la, la, la, la</i>
<i>La, la, la ♪</i>

1450
01:40:43,678 --> 01:40:49,149
<i>♪ La, la, la, la</i>
<i>La, la, la, la ♪</i>

1451
01:40:49,249 --> 01:40:54,321
<i>♪ La, la, la, la, la</i>
<i>La, la, la ♪</i>

1452
01:40:54,421 --> 01:40:59,661
<i>♪ You force your fire and then</i>
<i>You falsify your deeds ♪</i>

1453
01:40:59,761 --> 01:41:02,697
<i>♪ Your methods dot</i>
<i>The disconnect ♪</i>

1454
01:41:02,797 --> 01:41:05,265
<i>♪ From all your creeds ♪</i>

1455
01:41:05,365 --> 01:41:09,938
